 & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡{30}^{∘} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-120368/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2902b205-4508-55c6-9a68-f57d3afc9eab"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-120368"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-275706/field-1/b93157e0eb36ec8e645eeabaa0819400f448209e0db24c1abf59704822466393" :answer/id #uuid "46fb4a9c-5873-545c-a34d-b7e796bb3956" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-275706/field-1/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" :answer/id #uuid "0cab7834-6e8f-57ef-bacd-8e43fd0320e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-275706/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "06816d7f-60c7-52ec-bcb9-c62d20edf5e4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-275706/field-1/b93157e0eb36ec8e645eeabaa0819400f448209e0db24c1abf59704822466393" :answer-field/choices ["q-275706/field-1/b93157e0eb36ec8e645eeabaa0819400f448209e0db24c1abf59704822466393" "q-275706/field-1/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-275706" :question/id #uuid "db3cb6f0-7b3b-594b-92f6-3d97fd7b37dc" :question/math-academy-id "q-275706" :question/problem "Find the **exact** value of the expression below.\n\n${cos}^{4}⁡({15}^{∘})-2{cos}^{2}⁡({15}^{∘}){sin}^{2}⁡({15}^{∘})+{sin}^{4}⁡({15}^{∘})=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that our expression is a perfect square that can be rewritten as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{4}⁡({15}^{∘})-2{cos}^{2}⁡({15}^{∘}){sin}^{2}⁡({15}^{∘})+{sin}^{4}⁡({15}^{∘}) & ={({cos}^{2}⁡({15}^{∘})-{sin}^{2}⁡({15}^{∘}))}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x={15}^{∘}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{2}⁡({15}^{∘})-{sin}^{2}⁡({15}^{∘}) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot {15}^{∘}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡({30}^{∘}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{({cos}^{2}⁡({15}^{∘})-{sin}^{2}⁡({15}^{∘}))}^{2} & ={(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})}^{2}=\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-275706/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2902b205-4508-55c6-9a68-f57d3afc9eab"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-275706"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-332148/field-1/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "c397dc45-d133-5b1d-9f07-3a73216de451" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332148/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "7ffa1b88-eae6-5a01-a4be-ccf6bf9aca8e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-332148/field-1/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer-field/choices ["q-332148/field-1/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-332148" :question/id #uuid "24f718af-64bf-56f7-87f4-05511c65897e" :question/math-academy-id "q-332148" :question/problem "Find the **exact** value of the expression below.\n\n${cos}^{4}⁡({67.5}^{∘})-2{cos}^{2}⁡({67.5}^{∘}){sin}^{2}⁡({67.5}^{∘})+{sin}^{4}⁡({67.5}^{∘})=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that our expression is a perfect square that can be rewritten as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{4}⁡({67.5}^{∘})-2{cos}^{2}⁡({67.5}^{∘}){sin}^{2}⁡({67.5}^{∘})+{sin}^{4}⁡({67.5}^{∘}) & ={({cos}^{2}⁡({67.5}^{∘})-{sin}^{2}⁡({67.5}^{∘}))}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x={67.5}^{∘}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{2}⁡({67.5}^{∘})-{sin}^{2}⁡({67.5}^{∘}) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot {67.5}^{∘}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡({135}^{∘}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{({cos}^{2}⁡({67.5}^{∘})-{sin}^{2}⁡({67.5}^{∘}))}^{2} & ={(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})}^{2}=\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-332148/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2902b205-4508-55c6-9a68-f57d3afc9eab"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-332148"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
